== Correction, 20:20 NZDT (pointed out by the sentinel; the verdict above is unchanged, re-grading is not the tester's)
Step D's `show log | include -i secure|crypto|FIPS|verify` (work/stepD-u0.out, 20:17:51) returned TWO lines, and this log
quoted only the first. Both, verbatim:
2026 Oct 09 20:16:04 user.notice awplus IMI[683]: crypto secure-mode enabled
2026 Oct 09 20:16:04 user.warning awplus IMI[683]: Verification of the release file has failed, please verify it.
Together with the boot banner's "Please verify release with the 'crypto verify' command". The statement in step C that the
boot had "no error, failure or exception line" holds for the boot TRANSCRIPT only; the device log carries this warning.
Follow-up evidence (read-only, 20:19, recorded in T47115's run1.log): `show log permanent` holds the warning only for the
20:16:04 secure-mode boot, not for the earlier non-secure boots tonight; no `crypto verify` pair is configured. The x230
`crypto verify` page needs the release's SHA256 from the Download Center's sha256sum file, which this dev build
(awplus_main-20261008-57) does not have published; in secure mode a saved pair that fails would stop the unit booting, so
it was not attempted.
